      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-11-04_WidnesExaminer_art0139" n="art0139">
        <head>SALFORD AT WILDERSPOOL TO-DAY.</head>
        <p>SALFORD AT WILDERSPOOL TO-DAY.</p>
        <p>Warrington meet Salford at Wilderspool to-day, and followers are expecting a, victory. The kick-off is timed for 3 o'clock—hall an hour earlier than pre- vious matches. Warrington's team will be selected from: Horrocks; Baker, Tranter, Potter, Brookes, Griffiths; Nicholas, Young, Dainteth; Green, Harmer, Cunliffe, Matthews, Jones, Wall and Duin- bell. The visitors will select their team from no fewer than twenty-four players, viz.: W. H. La,unce, Driver R. M. Clifford, W. Thomas (capt.), A. Ains- worth, W. Robinson, G. W. Empson, W. D. John, E. Antrobus, J. Hampson, J. Baker. E. C. May, S. Costigan, B. Wanklyn, W. E. Clegg, E. Sykes, G. E. Currie, Bombardier E. Woods, J. Burgess, H. Dixon, T. Coates, Lce.-Corpl. J. Martindale, H. Whitney, A. Hindshaw and Sergt. W. Jones. 4</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON INTERMEDIATE LEAGUE. Result of Matches played October 28th. Rylands's, 26 points; Beamont, 2 points. Parochial, 27 points; St. Thomas', nil. Match for To.day. Heathside V. Rylands's, at Gorsey-lane. Kick-off 3 o'clock. Referee, Mr. J. Flynn.</p>
